From: fanboy <fanboy@openwrt.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:29:35 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: preserve TTL on bridge templates

airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare() sets AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TTL on every
flow entry, including bridge (L2) flows. A bridge must not decrement
the IPv4 TTL or IPv6 hop limit.

Gate the bit on non-bridge packet types, retaining the existing TTL
handling for routed flows. Bridge templates also seed learned IPv4/IPv6
L2 subflows, which must inherit the bridge policy.

Adapt the conditional TTL fix from fanboy's OpenW1700k commit to this
tree. This change does not alter flow classification or fix bridge
traffic that has already been classified as a routed flow.

Link: https://github.com/OpenWRT-fanboy/OpenW1700k/commit/e719630cc116e659384c6d7daa7d03d874391987
Signed-off-by: Dict Xiong <me@dxng.cn>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -441,8 +441,10 @@
 	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_UDP, l4proto == IPPROTO_UDP) |
 	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_VLAN_LAYER, data->vlan.num) |
 	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_VPM, data->vlan.num) |
-	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_PPPOE, data->pppoe.num) |
-	      AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TTL;
+	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_PPPOE, data->pppoe.num);
+	/* Bridge templates also seed IPv4/IPv6 L2 subflows. */
+	if (type != PPE_PKT_TYPE_BRIDGE)
+		val |= AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TTL;
 	hwe->ib1 = val;
 
 	val = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_PORT_AG, 0x1f);
